cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset or code, please cite the corresponding article."
title: "Surface Chemistry Effects on Molecular Transport in GO Membranes: Decoupling Geometric Confinement from Functional Group Affinity"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Gaona Cruz
    given-names: Oscar Javier
    affiliation: Universidad del Magdalena / University of Antwerp
repository-code: https://github.com/oscargaonacruz-design/GO-Chemistry-Desalination-MD
abstract: >
  Molecular dynamics simulation data and analysis scripts supporting the study of
  pressure-driven water transport and ion rejection in multilayer graphene oxide
  membranes. The repository isolates the role of surface chemistry by maintaining
  fixed geometric confinement while varying functional group type and density.
keywords:
  - graphene oxide
  - molecular dynamics
  - desalination
  - surface chemistry
  - ion rejection
license: MIT
date-released: 2025-01-01
